# overlay.env: defaults for the boxes this overlay provisions. provision sources it before it reads
# its flags, so a flag still wins. Copy this directory next to your own identity (or into a private
# repo) and point provision at it: --overlay DIR, or BOOTSTRAP_OVERLAY=DIR. docs/bootstrap.md has
# every setting and the hook contract. Everything here is commented out; nothing is needed.

# install.sh's identity and role for these boxes.
# BOOTSTRAP_IDENTITY=example
# BOOTSTRAP_ROLE=server

# More apt packages on top of the base set.
# BOOTSTRAP_APT_EXTRA="postgresql-client sqlite3"

# /etc/hosts lines, kept in a managed block (one per line).
# BOOTSTRAP_HOSTS_ENTRIES="203.0.113.10 git.example.com"

# Tailscale: tags to advertise, and Tailscale SSH (off unless set to 1). The auth key never goes
# here: pass a file with --tailscale-authkey-file, or BOOTSTRAP_TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY in the environment.
# BOOTSTRAP_TAILSCALE_TAGS=tag:server
# BOOTSTRAP_TAILSCALE_SSH=0

# The instance store: what goes on it, and the swap file's size in GB (0 for none).
# NVME_BINDS="/var/lib/docker /var/lib/containerd"
# NVME_SWAP_GB=8
